============================== Conclusion
1. An arbitrary topological order interleaves parallel regions and the pattern is MISSED.
2. Parallelism *inside* a block is harmless: the block stays contiguous either way.
3. Worse than missing: an arbitrary order can report a FALSE pattern (`AEBFCG` in case 3),
   an interleaving of two unrelated towers that is not a meaningful module at all.
-> The 1-D reduction needs a canonical, region-preserving topological order,
   and every candidate must still be verified by real sub-graph isomorphism.

